  "findings": [
    "Loss clusters around approximately18-19s and43-45s, while route5 also shows four-frame source-clock jumps at ordinary approximately20ms packet-arrival intervals.",
    "The only failed identity block is route0 at17.936-18.096s: five original packets span160ms. The expected920Hz tone has the highest measured power, but fails the existing8x spectral dominance requirement. This is not evidence of another identified source and is not a pass.",
    "Core records65explicit trimmed20ms chunks. Native ingress source audit finds that PortIngress maps temporary NotReady to Closed and NativePeerMedia::route consumes the datagram after is_ok(), with no owned retry. The fresh admission callback may synchronously retry authority-busy for up to10ms.",
    "Neither aggregate trim counters nor sender-report interpolation assigns every missing packet to a unique cause. Do not claim all audio loss is explained or change quality limits."
  ],
  "source_audit": [
    {
      "path": "crates/connect-service/src/canonical_media/packets.rs",
      "behavior": "Fresh publishing admission has a10ms synchronous retry budget; retained/receiving admissions use immediate reads."
    },
    {
      "path": ".deps/rvoip/crates/uctp/rvoip-uctp/src/staged_media.rs",
      "behavior": "PortIngress::publish_source calls try_publish_clocked once; Backpressure maps to Full, every other error maps to Closed."
    },
    {
      "path": ".deps/rvoip/crates/uctp/rvoip-uctp/src/v2/native_media.rs",
      "behavior": "The owned datagram reader invokes route synchronously and counts refusal; the exact refused frame is not retained for a bounded admission retry."
    },
    {
      "path": ".deps/rvoip/crates/foundation/rvoip-core/src/staged_streams/guarded_audio.rs",
      "behavior": "keep_next_original trims larger unplayed backlogs to two chunks; take/collect already retry unavailable current metadata through original queued owners."
    }
  ],
